  "notes": "The weighted table each world's points of interest are drawn from (design §6). Written by Claude; tune the weights freely. Lairs (one per threat in data/claude/threats.json, keyed by `threats`) are only drawn where their threat holds the land; they and the active dungeons (haunted barrow, kobold-held mine) are hostile and feed their domain's threat until cleared, about a quarter of all sites. Lone experts train a skill, sell what they know or heal; quest sites are placeholders for Plan 4 quests. Only springs and wells refill the waterskins (saint's well, herbwife's spring). Wonders are rarer than shrines and landmarks; the glass field is rarer still, as deserts are wide. Plan 6 D2: the three generic dungeons (haunted barrow, kobold-held mine, old ruin) have weight 0: the authored dungeons (data/claude/dungeons-*.json) replace them in new worlds, and they stay only for older saves.",
